-- title:
--   Each component of the special fibre of the edge chart is infinite
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, let $\pi \in \mathcal O$ be such that the principal ideal $(\pi)$ is maximal, and let $r \in \mathbb N$. Write $A :=$ `chartERing 𝒪 π r` for the localisation of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2,\mathcal O)/(\mathtt{edgeRel}\,\mathcal O\,\pi)$ away from the residue class `edgeQuot.discr 𝒪 π r` of the element $\mathtt{edgeDiscr}\,\mathcal O\,r$ of the two-variable polynomial ring, and let $A_0 := A/(\varphi(\pi)^{0+1})$ be the quotient of $A$ by the ideal generated by the $(0+1)$-st power of the image of $\pi$ under the structure map $\mathcal O \to A$; thus $A_0$ is the fibre of $A$ over the residue field $\mathcal O/(\pi)$. Let $\mathfrak p$ be an ideal of $A_0$ that is a minimal prime of $A_0$ (a minimal element of the set of primes of $A_0$). The conclusion is that the set of points $\mathfrak q$ of $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$ whose underlying prime ideal contains $\mathfrak p$ is infinite.
--
--   This is the statement that every irreducible component of the special fibre of the standard edge chart occurring in the Čerednik–Drinfeld / Mumford uniformisation carries infinitely many points; only the first level $\pi^{0+1}$ of the $\pi$-adic filtration is treated. It feeds the verification of the conditions on the special level of a Mumford glue datum, being cited by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordGlue.specialLevel_isField_isReduced_dim_infinite`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.MumfordGlue.specialLevel_isField_isReduced_dim_infinite).
